  "description": "Works to Trees in a Conservation Area: The works are part of a regular maintenance program to retain the trees at a suitable size for their location, encourage well balanced crowns for future years and an even distribution of growth throughout the crown\rRear Garden\rT1 Acacia: Remove 2 lowest limbs back to stem Liftto 3m and deadwood\rT2  Silver Birch: Remove lower branches back to stem Lift to 3m and any crossing branches\rT3  Eucalpytus: Reduce top by up to 2 metres\rT4  Pyracantha: Cut back longer laterals by 1.5 metres to form a more compact crown \rPoplar: remove 1 limb back to stem on the Poplar\rT5 & T6  Conifers: Cut back Conifer by 1.5 metres\rT7  Conifer: Fell Conifer \rLaurel: cut back Laurel to the fence line\rT8  Birch: Remove lower limbs Lift to 3m back to stem to make tree more upright\rT9  Purple Leaf Plum: Crown reduction by up to 2 metres of branch length\rT10 Birch: Remove lower limbs Liftto 3m back to stem to make tree more upright\r",
